{% set local_problem %}
<p>Decatur's mature neighborhoods mean serious debris accumulation. The historic areas around Bank Street and downtown feature large, established trees that drop leaves, seeds, and twigs constantly. Areas near Point Mallard are heavily wooded. Even newer subdivisions have enough tree coverage to keep gutters filling throughout the year.</p>

<p>The real problem isn't just clogged gutters — it's what happens when they overflow. Decatur sits along the Tennessee River, and that proximity means elevated water tables throughout much of the city. When gutters send water toward your foundation instead of away from it, that water often has nowhere to go. It pools, saturates the soil, and eventually finds its way into your basement or crawlspace.</p>

<p>Morgan County's red clay soil makes this worse. Clay doesn't absorb water well, so overflow from clogged gutters sits against your foundation rather than draining away. Over time, this causes cracks, leaks, and structural damage that costs thousands to repair.</p>

<p>Regular gutter cleaning prevents all of this. It's one of the most cost-effective ways to protect your Decatur home from water damage.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We start by hand-removing all debris from inside your gutters — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, decomposed organic matter, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are a common problem that many homeowners miss when attempting DIY cleaning — debris backs up in the downspout, water can't exit, and the gutter overflows even though it looks clean from above.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system: hangers, seams, slope, and the fascia boards behind. We'll flag loose hangers, developing leaks, rust spots, and fascia damage before they become expensive problems. When we're done, we clean up all debris from your landscaping.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters throughout Decatur and Morgan County for over 20 years. From historic downtown homes with complex rooflines to modern construction, we've handled every gutter configuration and debris challenge this area presents.</p>

<p>Based just 25 minutes away in Huntsville, we're close enough to respond quickly and local enough to care about doing the job right. When you call Blue River Gutters, you're talking to people who know Decatur — not a call center in another state.</p>
